try {
    processRequest();
} catch (Exception e) {           // recoverable conditions only
    log.error("request failed", e);
    return errorResponse(e);
}
// OutOfMemoryError / StackOverflowError are NOT caught here.
// They propagate up and let the process fail fast and restart clean.
```
*Catching `Exception` keeps `Error` propagating, which is exactly what you want when the JVM is dying.*

