public class OrderService {
    // No 'throws' needed for unchecked exceptions
    public Order createOrder(Long userId, List<String> items) {
        if (userId == null)
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("userId must not be null");
        if (items.isEmpty())
            throw new IllegalStateException("order needs at least one item");
        return new Order(userId, items);
    }

    // A checked exception DOES force a throws declaration
    public String readNotes(String path) throws java.io.IOException {
        return java.nio.file.Files.readString(java.nio.file.Path.of(path));
    }
}
```
*`IllegalArgumentException`/`IllegalStateException` are unchecked; the caller is free to ignore them because they indicate misuse — a bug.*

