```java
try {
    repository.save(order);
} catch (SQLException e) {
    // Pass the original as the cause -> getCause() returns it later.
    throw new OrderSaveException("could not save order", e);
}

// Reading the chain when handling:
catch (OrderSaveException ex) {
    log.error("save failed: {}", ex.getMessage(), ex);   // logs full chain
    Throwable root = ex.getCause();                      // the SQLException
}
```
*The log now shows `Caused by: java.sql.SQLException ...` with the real database error code.*

```java
public class FinallyDemo {
    int withReturn() {
        try {
            return 1;                 // value computed...
        } finally {
            System.out.println("runs before the method returns");
        }
    }

    void uncaught() {
        try {
            throw new RuntimeException("boom");  // no catch here
        } finally {
            System.out.println("still runs, THEN boom propagates");
        }
    }

    void exits() {
        try {
            System.exit(0);           // JVM stops immediately
        } finally {
            System.out.println("NEVER prints");
        }
    }
}
